{
  "title": "iFuse TORQ TNT®",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/implants/423359/ifuse-torq-tnt-r-",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 18 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The iFuse TORQ TNT® Implant System is indicated for pelvic fracture fixation and sacroiliac joint fusion to address acute or non-traumatic fractures and chronic joint dysfunction.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "It achieves this through a cannulated, pin-based workflow utilizing a 3D-printed porous threaded implant designed for transiliac-transsacral trajectories to maximize osseointegration and pelvic ring stability.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "This versatile platform provides immediate mechanical fixation with TORQLock™ hooked threads while leveraging navigation or fluoroscopic guidance to navigate narrow sacral corridors.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Related Implants",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "iFuse TORQ® Implant Family",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "iFuse Implant System® Family",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Sacropelvic Solutions™ Portfolio",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pelvic fracture fixation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "fracture fixation of the pelvis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "acute fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "non-acute fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "non-traumatic fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Sacroiliac joint fusion",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "sacroiliac joint fusion for sacroiliac joint dysfunction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "sacroiliac joint disruption",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "degenerative sacroiliitis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "posterior pelvic ring includes sacrum, ilium, and sacroiliac articulation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "sacral ala and sacral body define the osseous corridor for S1 or S2 fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "sacral canal, sacral foramina, anterior sacral cortex, and iliac cortices define key safety boundaries",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Muscles",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "gluteal musculature and posterior soft tissues are traversed or dilated",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "gluteus maximus fibers may be spread during blunt dissection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ligaments",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "anterior sacroiliac ligaments",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "interosseous sacroiliac ligaments",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "posterior sacroiliac ligaments",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Nerves",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "sacral nerve roots are at risk during pin, drill, tap, and implant advancement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "S1 foramen is a key fluoroscopic landmark for S1 corridor placement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "S2 foramen is relevant for outlet view assessment and S2 corridor planning",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Blood supply",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "superior gluteal artery and surrounding neurovascular structures are at risk during incision and deep dissection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "iliolumbar and lateral sacral vascular branches may be encountered near posterior pelvic ring corridors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approach",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Positioning",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "supine or prone positioning may be used",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "keep SI joint neutral without extreme hip flexion or extension",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Preoperative planning",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "CT is recommended for preoperative planning",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "assess sacral corridor width, sacral dysmorphism, foraminal position, sacral canal, and fracture morphology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Fluoroscopic imaging",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inlet view optimizes visualization of anterior sacral cortex and S1 body alignment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "outlet view optimizes visualization of S1 and S2 neuroforamina",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Skin marking",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423359/images/972360c8-828e-4a87-93fd-c9abf7176dbd_screenshot_2026-05-14_at_5.06.20_pm.jpg",
              "caption": "First Skin Marking"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mark a line from ASIS toward the floor in supine position",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "mark a transverse line in line with the center of the femur extending posteriorly",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Sacral style trajectory",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "placed in transverse orientation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "oriented orthogonal to a vertical sacral fracture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "SI style trajectory",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "placed orthogonal to the SI joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "commonly starts posterior-superior on the ilium",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "commonly terminates in anterior-inferior sacrum",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "First pin placement",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "insert preferred 2.5 mm pin into ilium to desired depth",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423359/images/ef33f7a3-189b-49dc-bee7-37c33970e2b1_screenshot_2026-05-14_at_5.09.33_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "Insert preferred 2.5 mm pin into ilium to desired depth"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "advance under alternating inlet and outlet views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "ensure pin crosses fracture site when fixing fracture to reduce displacement risk during implant insertion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Dilation and implant length determination",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "slide and rotate Dilator over pin until distal tip contacts ilium",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423359/images/b5f5f363-570f-4928-b7d4-cb9b7cc18372_screenshot_2026-05-14_at_5.12.07_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "Slide and rotate Dilator over pin until distal tip contacts ilium"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "avoid aggressive insertion to reduce instrument, bone, or tissue damage",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "STP and drill sleeve placement",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "press Drill Sleeve into STP until seated",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "slide STP with Drill Sleeve over Dilator until STP tip contacts ilium",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423359/images/85a4424d-ddc8-4a26-bb57-f1b7d741b71c_screenshot_2026-05-14_at_5.12.51_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "Slide STP with Drill Sleeve over Dilator until STP tip contacts ilium"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "remove Dilator after STP and Drill Sleeve are in position",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "maintain STP position through drilling, tapping, and implantation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Drill sleeve removal",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "remove Drill Sleeve from STP before implant insertion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423359/images/feae5f3f-8107-43e6-aa2a-4b0b4c4a0261_screenshot_2026-05-14_at_5.13.36_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "Remove Drill Sleeve from STP before implant insertion"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "press gold tabs to release Drill Sleeve",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "maintain STP position while removing Drill Sleeve",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Implant transfer",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "confirm implant size from tube label",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "maintain sterility of threaded implant tube and TPU sleeve",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "advance outer sleeve onto implant using two-finger tightness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "remove loaded Driver-Implant assembly from TPU sleeve",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Implant insertion",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "advance implant on Locking Driver using power with Quarter Inch to Tri-Lobe Adapter or by hand with T-Handle or Inline Handle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423359/images/02b72a5a-6ad6-41ce-b790-3a2a71cc21a2_screenshot_2026-05-14_at_5.14.18_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "Advance implant on Locking Driver using power with Quarter Inch to Tri-Lobe Adapter or by hand with T-Handle or Inline Handle"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "final implant seating should be performed manually",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "use laser mark on Driver relative to proximal STP to estimate head position when Driver and STP are used together",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "if SI joint fusion is desired, place iFuse TORQ TNT® along with one or more additional implants across SI joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "if implant becomes difficult to advance in hard bone, remove implant and drill and tap to prepare bone channel",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Final fluoroscopic confirmation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "obtain final inlet, outlet, and lateral views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "confirm fracture implant has adequately crossed fracture site",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423359/images/747146cf-be17-47b2-8873-d5e75fa3e5b7_screenshot_2026-05-14_at_5.15.15_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "Confirm fracture implant has adequately crossed fracture site"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Closure",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "close using standard technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Implant removal",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "clear debris obstructing implant T40 Torx head",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "place pin through implant",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "insert driver over pin and engage implant",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technical specifications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
